<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Posen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1806</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-fourth-coalition">War of the Fourth Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poznan">Posen</a>, signed on 11 December 1806 at Posen (Poznań), made peace between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> and Elector <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-augustus-iii-of-saxony">Frederick Augustus III of Saxony</a>, who had fought on the Prussian side at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jena">Jena</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/confederation-of-the-rhine">Confederation of the Rhine</a>, its ruler took the title of king as Frederick Augustus I, and Catholics in Saxony received equal rights with Lutherans.</p></div>
